/// DOM backend for the `embed` device — merged under `[select] embed = "dom"`. One <iframe> (ekind 0) or
/// <a><img></a> (ekind 1) per `bid`, absolutely positioned over the gfx <canvas>. Like textview/dom there is NO
/// C shim: `embed_be_*` stay undefined and become wasm IMPORTS the JS host (co-located host.js) fulfils. The
/// seams are `#module`-private. Not a standalone test.
///
/// TWO seams, not one proc with two string params: a foreign proc borrows ONE `[]char` cleanly (the same idiom
/// gfx uses for the framebuffer), so the click-through link gets its own call — exactly how `panel` splits
/// `panel_be_render` from `panel_be_sub`. `render` re-issues both every frame (an idempotent redraw), so a card
/// whose `screen`/`size` the driver reprojects per frame tracks the scrolling world.
#module
#foreign
embed_be_render :: proc(bid: int, src: []char, n: int, kind: int, x: int, y: int, w: int, h: int)(src: []char);
// OPENING the real site is not the card's job — a card is not a link. The driver owns a `button` row per card
// (the same device the playground's RUN uses), reads its `clicked`, and raises `eopen` for one frame. This is
// the only seam that knows what a URL is.
embed_be_open   :: proc(link: []char, n: int)(link: []char);
// A card is a real DOM element sitting ABOVE the gfx <canvas>, so a click on it never reaches gfx's canvas
// mouse listeners — the driver's screen-rect hit test can never see it. The host knows, though: the browser
// focuses the element that was clicked. So focus crosses back as a COLUMN the driver reads, exactly like
// button's `clicked` — "a producer writes a column, a consumer reads it". Same shape as gfx's `text_focus`,
// which is how the playground's editor tells the driver it took the keyboard.
#foreign
embed_be_focused :: proc(bid: int)(f: int);

/// Place/size every card.
render :: system eff {
  map (query { bid, esrc, elen, ekind, screen, size }) eff {
    embed_be_render(bid, esrc, elen, ekind, screen.x, screen.y, size.w, size.h)(_:);
  };
}

/// `eopen` is the driver's one-frame "open this card's site" — it is a CONSUMER of the Button device's
/// `clicked`, exactly as the playground's RUN is. An empty `elink` means the card has nowhere to go.
open :: system eff {
  map (query { eopen, elink, ellen }) eff {
    if (eopen == 1) {
      embed_be_open(elink, ellen)(_:);
    }
  };
}

/// `efocus` = does this card hold the browser's focus right now (i.e. the visitor clicked into it).
poll :: system eff {
  map (query { bid, efocus })(efocus) eff {
    embed_be_focused(bid)(f:);
    efocus = f;
  };
}
